.TH "WINDOW.DEVICEORIENTATIONABSOLUTE_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Window.deviceorientationabsolute_event \- Window:
deviceorientationabsolute event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]deviceorientationabsolute\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when
absolute device orientation changes.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqdeviceorientationabsolute\(dq, (event) => { })

ondeviceorientationabsolute = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]DeviceOrientationEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
